+// Counts the elements and child slots the clone of one transition's subtree needs (breadth first, as the clone
+// itself walks it). False when the subtree reaches outside this frame's elements or children, which a clone must not
+// read: the clones are written downwards from the top of the arrays and could overwrite such a source first.
